<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  LaunchAgent for the daily off-box pull of the pool's history.

  WHAT IT CLOSES
    docs/THREAT_MODEL.md's third open item, and the first of the two gaps
    docs/ASVS-L2.md names as the ones that would actually hurt. bin/backup
    writes a nightly tarball to the VM's own local disk — the one place
    guaranteed to fail separately from the Azure Files share, which is what it
    was for, and not separately from the VM. This machine is off-box. That is
    the whole argument.

  WHY launchd AND NOT cron
    macOS enters "Maintenance Sleep" even on a desktop wired to AC, and cron
    does NOT fire while the system is asleep — so a 04:10 cron line is a backup
    that silently does not happen on the nights it matters. launchd's
    StartCalendarInterval reschedules the job for the next wake. (Same reason
    the poker-manager backup moved off cron.)

  WHY 04:10 LOCAL
    bin/backup runs on the server at 02:40 UTC, which is 19:40 or 20:40 the
    previous evening here. 04:10 local is several hours after that whatever the
    daylight-saving offset is doing, so this never races the job it copies —
    and if it ever does, pull-backup.sh grades the SERVER tarball's age and
    says so rather than reporting a successful copy of yesterday's.

  THE ONE THING THAT NEEDS A PERSON
    The server is reached with an Entra SSH certificate minted by
    `az ssh config`, and it is valid for about an hour — so every run mints a
    fresh one. That works unattended for as long as the Azure CLI can refresh
    its own token silently, and stops working when it cannot: a tenant policy,
    a password change, a revoked session. pull-backup.sh then exits non-zero
    with "not logged in to Azure — run: az login" rather than warning, and
    `./deploy/pull-backup.sh --check` is the thing that notices the copies have
    stopped arriving. A backup that quietly stopped is the failure this whole
    project has a paragraph about; put --check somewhere you read.

  Install:
    mkdir -p ~/Library/LaunchAgents
    cp deploy/launchd/com.poolhound.backup-pull.plist ~/Library/LaunchAgents/
    launchctl load -w ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.poolhound.backup-pull.plist

  Verify scheduled:
    launchctl list | grep poolhound.backup-pull
    launchctl print gui/$(id -u)/com.poolhound.backup-pull | grep -iE 'next fire|last exit'

  Run on demand (smoke test):
    launchctl kickstart -k gui/$(id -u)/com.poolhound.backup-pull
    ./deploy/pull-backup.sh --check

  Uninstall:
    launchctl unload -w ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.poolhound.backup-pull.plist
    rm ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.poolhound.backup-pull.plist
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>Label</key>
    <string>com.poolhound.backup-pull</string>

    <key>ProgramArguments</key>
    <array>
        <string>/Users/jacobc/code/poolhound/deploy/pull-backup.sh</string>
    </array>

    <key>StartCalendarInterval</key>
    <dict>
        <key>Hour</key>
        <integer>4</integer>
        <key>Minute</key>
        <integer>10</integer>
    </dict>

    <key>WorkingDirectory</key>
    <string>/Users/jacobc/code/poolhound</string>

    <!-- launchd gives a job a minimal PATH that has neither Homebrew nor the
         Azure CLI in it, and the script's first act is `command -v az`. This
         mirrors the PATH an interactive shell would have handed it; az lives
         in /opt/homebrew/bin on Apple Silicon. -->
    <key>EnvironmentVariables</key>
    <dict>
        <key>PATH</key>
        <string>/opt/homebrew/bin:/opt/homebrew/sbin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/sbin</string>
    </dict>

    <!-- The script prints a dated banner and one line per step, so these two
         files ARE the log. Outside the checkout, beside the backups, because
         this tree is published and the log names the server. Appended to by
         launchd, never rotated by it — which is fine at a few hundred bytes a
         day and is worth knowing. -->
    <key>StandardOutPath</key>
    <string>/Users/jacobc/Backups/poolhound/pull.log</string>
    <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
    <string>/Users/jacobc/Backups/poolhound/pull.err</string>

    <!-- A periodic job, not a daemon: do not restart it when it exits, and do
         not run it the moment this agent loads. The smoke test above is how
         you run it now. -->
    <key>RunAtLoad</key>
    <false/>
</dict>
</plist>
